Auf der Maur is the eponymous debut studio album by the Canadian alternative rock musician Melissa Auf der Maur, released on February 2, 2004 on Capitol Records.  Following her career as a bassist for Hole and The Smashing Pumpkins, Auf der Maur recorded the album of the course of two years in various studios through the United States and Canada with producer Chris Goss.  The songs featured on ""Auf der Maur"" were written over a ten-year period, from 1992 to 2002, throughout her time in Tinker,

