## Mutulu Shakur
Mutulu Shakur (born Jeral Wayne Williams; August 8, 1950) is an American black Revolutionary.  He was a proponent of the Republic of New Afrika and a close friend of Geronimo Pratt.

---

The Black Liberation Army (BLA) was an underground, black nationalist militant organization that operated in the United States from 1970 to 1981.  Composed largely of former Black Panthers (BPP), the organization's program was one of armed struggle against the United States Government, and its stated goal was to ""take up arms for the liberation and self-determination of black people in the United States.""  The BLA carried out a series of bombings, killings of police officers and drug dealers,

