naive,recursive,qwen3.5:0.8b,What animated shorts were both worked on by Irven Spence and distributed by an American media company?,Tom and Jerry,"Irven Spence is credited with creating ""Texas Tom"" in 1950 and ""Smarty Cat"" in 1955, both of which were distributed by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer. Additionally, both shorts were animated by Irven Spence alongside Ray Patterson and Kenneth Muse. The other shorts listed in the context, such as ""Little Runaway"" (1952), ""Mouse Trouble"" (1944), and the earlier ""Smitten Kitten,"" were animated by a different team (including Ken Muse and others) and were produced by Fred Quimby, not distributed by MGM.",0.03389830508474576,False,2.0,3.0,2.0,2.3333333333333335,6837.649099999908,2.0,2.0,2.0,2.0,2329.6903000000384,2.166666666666667,1256.7647000005309,9167.339399999946,10424.104100000477,"## Irven Spence
