## Belmont, Massachusetts
Belmont is a town in Middlesex County, Massachusetts, a western suburb of Boston.  It is part of the greater Boston metropolitan area.  Its population was 26,171 as of 01 2016

---

## Levi S. Gould
Levi Swanton Gould (March 27, 1831 – March 22, 1917) was an American businessman and politician who served as a member, and chairman of the Middlesex County, Massachusetts county commission, and as the first mayor of Melrose, Massachusetts.

---

## Storrow Drive
Storrow Drive is a major crosstown parkway in Boston, Massachusetts, running east and north along the Charles River to Leverett Circle.  It is restricted to cars; trucks and buses are not permitted on it.  The road, legally known as James Jackson Storrow Memorial Drive, officially ends at its eastward junction with Route 28 (near Arlington Street) and continues as David G. Mugar Way (formerly Embankment Road), concurrent with Route 28.

---

---

## David G. Booth
David G. Booth (born 1946) is an American businessman.  He is the co-founder and co-CEO of Dimensional Fund Advisors (along with Rex Sinquefield and Eduardo Repetto, respectively).  In 2008, he donated $300 million to the University of Chicago Graduate School of Business (equivalent to $ million in 2016 ), which is the largest donation ever given to a business school.

