Giuseppe Tornatore (born 27 May 1956) is an Italian film director and screenwriter.  He is considered as one of the directors who brought critical acclaim back to Italian cinema.  In a career spanning over 30 years he is best known for directing and writing drama films such as ""The Legend of 1900"", ""Malèna"", ""Baarìa"" and ""The Best Offer"".  Probably his most noted film is ""Nuovo Cinema Paradiso"", for which Tornatore won the Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film.  He directed also several

