The Indian Professional Boxing Association (Hindi: भारतीय पेशेवर मुक्केबाजी संघ ) is the National Governing Body for Professional Boxing in India, which sanctions professional boxing matches and awards national and subordinate championship titles.  IPBA is a member organization of the World Boxing Association (WBA), the World Boxing Organization (WBO), the International Boxing Federation (IBF) and the Pan Asian Boxing Association (PABA).  It is headquartered in New Delhi, India.

A weight class is a measurement weight range for boxers.  The lower limit of a weight class is equal to the upper weight limit of the class below it.  The top class, with no upper limit, is called heavyweight in professional boxing and super heavyweight in amateur boxing.  A boxing match is usually scheduled for a fixed weight class, and each boxer's weight must not exceed the upper limit.  Although professional boxers may fight above their weight class, an amateur boxer's weight must not fall

