The Paso Fino is a naturally gaited light horse breed dating back to horses imported to the Caribbean from Spain.  Pasos are prized for their smooth, natural, four-beat, lateral ambling gait; they are used in many disciplines, but are especially popular for trail riding.  In the United States two main groups of horses are popularly called ""Paso Fino"": One, also known as the Pure Puerto Rican Paso Fino (PPR), originated in Puerto Rico.  The other, often called the Colombian Paso Fino or

