## Willie &quot;Woo Woo&quot; Wong
Willie Wong () (1926 - 2005) was an American basketball player who was born and raised in Chinatown, San Francisco.  Though Wong was only 5'5"" tall, he excelled, and was known as one of the finest Chinese American basketball players in the 1940s.  He was nicknamed Willie ""Woo Woo"" Wong by a local sportswriter because fans would shout ""Woo Woo"" when he scored.

