Aladdin is a 1992 American animated comedy musical romantic fantasy adventure film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation for Walt Disney Pictures.  The film is the 31st Disney animated feature film, and was the fourth produced during the Disney film era known as the Disney Renaissance.  It was directed by John Musker and Ron Clements, and is based on the Arab-style folktale of the same name from ""One Thousand and One Nights"" and the French interpretation by Antoine Galland.  The voice cast

