## Akhil Bharatiya Sena
Akhil Bharatiya Sena (""lit.""  All India Army) is a political party in India.  Founded in 1997 and led by the Mumbai mafia don and contract killer Arun Gawli (alias 'Daddy').  Gawli had earlier been close to the Shiv Sena supremo, Bal Thackeray, but in 1996 a bloody feud surged between them when Arun Gawli mercilessly slew several Sena party legislators and party workers.  Gawli organized ABS as a counterwight to SS.

---

Arun Gulabrao Ahir or Arun Gawli is an Indian politician , underworld don and former gangster.  Gawli and his brother Kishor (Pappa) entered the Mumbai underworld in the 1970s when they joined the ""Byculla Company"", a criminal gang led by Rama Naik and Babu Reshim, operating in the central Mumbai areas of Byculla, Parel and Saat Rasta.  In 1988, after Rama Naik was killed in a police encounter, Gawli took over the gang and began operating it from his residence, Dagdi Chawl.  Under his control,

