## Retrospect for Life
""Retrospect for Life"" is the first single from rapper Common's third album ""One Day It'll All Make Sense"". It features production from James Poyser and No I.D., vocals from Lauryn Hill and bass guitar playing by Vere Isaacs. Its autobiographical lyrics weigh the choices of abortion and birth for a woman impregnated by Common. The lyrics as well as a ""mellow, piano-driven beat"" has caused Dan Menella to call it the most memorable track on Common's third album.

