## Puerto Rican citizenship
Puerto Rican citizenship was first legislated by the United States Congress in Article 7 of the Foraker Act of 1900 and later recognized in the Constitution of Puerto Rico. Puerto Rican citizenship existed before the U.S. takeover of the islands of Puerto Rico and continued afterwards.",none,n/a,substring,True,True,True,sentence,,,12,ollama,mxbai-embed-large,1024,hybrid,5,5,3209,,,ollama,local,qwen3.5:0.8b,Q8_0,hotpotqa,42
