naive,recursive,qwen3.5:2b,What historic province of Ireland is home to the 2017 Antrim Senior Football Championship and County Antrim?,Ulster,"County Antrim is part of the historic province of Ulster, which is home to the 2017 Antrim Senior Football Championship and the county itself.",0.0,True,5.0,5.0,4.0,4.666666666666667,2745.81820000094,5.0,5.0,5.0,5.0,1145.190300001559,4.833333333333334,760.5269999985467,3891.008500002499,4651.535500001046,"County Antrim (named after the town of Antrim, from Irish: ""Aontroim"" , meaning ""lone ridge"" , )) is one of six counties that form Northern Ireland.  Adjoined to the north-east shore of Lough Neagh, the county covers an area of 3046 km2 and has a population of about 618,000.  County Antrim has a population density of 203 people per square kilometer / 526 people per square mile.  It is also one of the thirty-two traditional counties of Ireland, as well as part of the historic province of Ulster.

