Giovanni Domenico Cappellino (1580–1651) was an Italian painter of the Renaissance period, active mainly in his natal city of Genoa.  He was the pupil of the painter Giovanni Battista Paggi.  At age 22, he painted a ""Saint Sebastian"" for the church of Santa Sabina.  He contributed a canvas to the Oratory of San Giacomo della Marina.  In Genoa, he painted a ""Death of St. Francis"" for the church of San Niccolo, and a ""St. Francesca Romana"" for the church of San Stefano.",none,n/a,substring,True,True,True,recursive,500,100,19,ollama,mxbai-embed-large,1024,hybrid,5,5,2267,,,ollama,local,qwen3.5:2b,Q8_0,hotpotqa,42
