Edward Charles ""Ed"" Hugler (born February 7, 1950) is Deputy Assistant Secretary for Operations in the U.S. Department of Labor's Office of the Assistant Secretary for Administration and Management.  That position has been his formal position at the United States Department of Labor since April 2000.  However, he served as Acting Secretary of Labor from February 2–24, 2009, when Hilda Solis's nomination by President Barack Obama became bogged down during Senate confirmation hearings.  He",generation,high,substring,True,True,True,recursive,500,100,34,ollama,mxbai-embed-large,1024,hybrid,5,5,1780,,,ollama,local,qwen3.5:2b,Q8_0,hotpotqa,42
