Hoddesdon is a town in the Broxbourne borough of the English county of Hertfordshire, situated in the Lea Valley.  It grew up as a coaching stop on the route between Cambridge and London.  It is located 3 mi West of Harlow 4 mi southeast of Hertford, 5 mi north of Waltham Cross and 11 mi southwest of Bishop's Stortford.  At its height during the 18th century, more than 35 coaches a day passed through the town.  It saw a boom in the mid 20th century as gravel was extracted from the area, but was",none,n/a,substring,True,True,True,recursive,500,100,13,ollama,mxbai-embed-large,1024,hybrid,5,5,1794,,,ollama,local,qwen3.5:2b,Q8_0,hotpotqa,42
