## Gregory Hoblit
Gregory King Hoblit (born November 27, 1944) is an American film director, television director and television producer.  He is known for directing the critically acclaimed films ""Primal Fear"", ""Frequency"" and ""Fracture"".  He has won nine Primetime Emmy Awards for directing and producing ""Hill Street Blues"", ""NYPD Blue"", ""L.A. Law"", ""Hooperman"" and the television film ""Roe vs. Wade"".

---

## Primal Fear (film)
Primal Fear is a 1996 American neo-noir crime-thriller film, based on William Diehl's 1993 novel of the same name and directed by Gregory Hoblit.

---

Fallen is a 1998 American supernatural detective thriller film directed by Gregory Hoblit, produced by Charles Roven and Dawn Steel, from a screenplay by Nicholas Kazan.  The film tells the story of John Hobbes, a Philadelphia police detective who is investigating murders committed by an apparent copycat killer.  The murderer is later revealed to be a fallen angel known as Azazel, who possesses human beings by touch.  Denzel Washington, Embeth Davidtz, James Gandolfini, John Goodman, Donald

---

## Roe vs. Wade (film)
Roe vs. Wade is a 1989 television film about the landmark 1973 United States Supreme Court decision ""Roe v. Wade"" written by Alison Cross.  It was directed by Gregory Hoblit and stars Holly Hunter.

