The Elkhead Mountains are a mountain range in Colorado.  The mountain range is considered to be low altitude within Colorado as the mountains are under 11000 ft .  Located within Routt and Moffat counties, the mountain range is far from metropolitan areas and has few lakes and streams, so it attracts few visitors.  The mountain range is a volcanic range and all of the peaks were formed by volcanic action.  The mountain range extends approximately 16 mi east to west and 10 mi north to south, and",none,n/a,substring,True,True,True,recursive,500,100,30,ollama,mxbai-embed-large,1024,hybrid,5,5,1915,,,ollama,local,qwen3.5:2b,Q8_0,hotpotqa,42
