## Oakland International Airport station
Oakland International Airport station is a Bay Area Rapid Transit (BART) station on the Coliseum–Oakland International Airport line in Oakland, California, United States.  This station is on the system's Automated Guideway Transit (AGT) spur line, which carries passengers between Oakland International Airport (OAK) and Oakland Coliseum Station.

---

## Coliseum–Oakland International Airport line
The Coliseum–Oakland International Airport line, also known informally as the BART to OAK line, is an automated guideway transit (AGT) system operated by Bay Area Rapid Transit (BART) between BART's Coliseum Station and Oakland International Airport.  The system opened for revenue service on November 22, 2014 and is integrated into BART’s fare system.  During planning and construction, it was known as the Oakland Airport Connector (OAC) project.",none,n/a,substring,True,True,True,recursive,500,100,22,ollama,mxbai-embed-large,1024,hybrid,5,5,1843,,,ollama,local,qwen3.5:2b,Q8_0,hotpotqa,42
