The Bayport Container Terminal, or simply the Bayport Terminal, is a major deep water port in the Greater Houston area in Texas (United States).  This relatively new terminal, part of the Port of Houston, is designed to handle standardized cargo containers and offload the nearby Barbours Cut Terminal, which has no further room for expansion.  The Bayport Terminal is situated along the Bayport Ship Channel off Galveston Bay, between La Porte, Texas and Seabrook, Texas (adjacent to Shoreacres and",none,n/a,substring,True,True,True,recursive,500,100,26,ollama,mxbai-embed-large,1024,hybrid,5,5,1770,,,ollama,local,qwen3.5:2b,Q8_0,hotpotqa,42
