## Danny McBride
Daniel Richard McBride (born December 29, 1976) is an American actor, writer, and comedian.  He is best known for starring in the HBO comedies ""Eastbound & Down"" and ""Vice Principals"", both of which he co-created with frequent collaborator Jody Hill.  He has also starred in comedy films, such as ""The Foot Fist Way"" (2006), ""Hot Rod"" (2007), ""Pineapple Express"" (2008), ""Tropic Thunder"" (2008), ""Land of the Lost"" (2009), ""Your Highness"" (2011), and ""This Is the End"" (2013).

