## Wendell Potter
Wendell Potter (born July 16, 1951) is an American consumer advocate, ""New York Times"" bestselling author, consultant, and former health insurance industry executive. A critic of HMOs and of the tactics used by insurers, Potter is also an advocate for major reforms of the industry, including universal health care.

