The context states that Leo Strauss ""specialized in **classical political philosophy**."" It also identifies Robert Locke as an admirer of Strauss and confirms his background as the American conservative columnist mentioned in the question.",0.05263157894736842,True,5.0,5.0,4.0,4.666666666666667,3070.15180000235,5.0,5.0,5.0,5.0,1165.503300002456,4.833333333333334,912.3844999994617,4235.655100004806,5148.039600004267,"He was born in Germany to Jewish parents and later emigrated from Germany to the United States. He spent most of his career as a professor of political science at the University of Chicago, where he taught several generations of students and published fifteen books. ---

## Laurence Lampert
Laurence Lampert (born 1941) is a Canadian philosopher and a leading scholar in the field of Nietzsche studies. He is also well known for his interpretation of the German-American political philosopher, Leo Strauss. ---

## Robert Locke (disambiguation)
Robert Locke is an editor and American conservative.

---

## Robert P. George
Robert Peter George (born July 10, 1955) is an American legal scholar, political philosopher, and public intellectual who serves as the McCormick Professor of Jurisprudence at Princeton University. He lectures on constitutional interpretation, civil liberties, philosophy of law, and political philosophy. George, a Roman Catholic, is considered one of the country's leading conservative intellectuals. ---

## Leo Strauss
Leo Strauss ( ; ] ; September 20, 1899 – October 18, 1973) was a German-American political philosopher and classicist who specialized in classical political philosophy.

He was the founding president of the National Association of Scholars from 1987 to 2009. ---

## Robert Locke
Robert Locke is an American conservative columnist. Locke has attended both Columbia University and University of Chicago. He is critical of liberals, libertarians, and some ""compassionate conservatives"", including George W. Bush.

He is an admirer of conservative scholar Leo Strauss, architect Robert A.M. Stern, and photorealist painter Richard Estes. He was a columnist in ""FrontPage Magazine"" until February 2003.

---

## History of Political Philosophy
History of Political Philosophy is a textbook edited by American political philosophers Leo Strauss and Joseph Cropsey. This book is intended primarily to introduce undergraduate students of political science to political philosophy. It is currently in its third edition. ---

## Stephen Balch
Stephen H. Balch is an American conservative scholar and higher education reformer.",none,n/a,substring,True,True,True,sentence,,,8,ollama,mxbai-embed-large,1024,hybrid,5,5,2165,,,ollama,local,qwen3.5:2b,Q8_0,hotpotqa,42
