## 1994–95 Cleveland Cavaliers season
The 1994–95 NBA season was the 25th season of the National Basketball Association for the franchise based in Cleveland, Ohio. This was also the team's first season playing at the Gund Arena. During the offseason, the Cavaliers signed unrestricted free agent Michael Cage. Despite losing Brad Daugherty and Gerald Wilkins for the entire season to injuries, and Mark Price for 34 games with a broken wrist, the Cavaliers posted an 11-game winning streak in December which led them to a 20–8 start.",none,n/a,substring,True,True,True,sentence,,,13,ollama,mxbai-embed-large,1024,hybrid,5,5,3765,,,ollama,local,qwen3.5:2b,Q8_0,hotpotqa,42
