He has also been nominated three further times, including two nominations in the same category for ""The Decline of the American Empire"" in 1986 and ""Jesus of Montreal"" in 1989, becoming the only French-Canadian director in history to receive this number of nominations and, subsequently, to win the award. Also for ""The Barbarian Invasions"", he received an Academy Award nomination for Best Original Screenplay, losing to Sofia Coppola for ""Lost in Translation"".

